## ROOT CAUSE

FIX-I was measured only on the 5 sentences that motivated it. The campaign's own new standing rule **(d)** says widening a rescue must be measured on its false-positive corpus; FIX-I *narrows* a rescue, and the mirror of the rule was never applied. `run27`'s D156/D162b pins are all **linker-free**, so the last disjunct rescues them before the evidential arm is reached — **the suite is structurally incapable of observing FIX-I's cost.** Same shape for FIX-H: the D161 hedge corpus is built entirely from lexicon words.

**Seventh consecutive campaign** in which a two-directional trade is reported as one-directional — and the first where a single one-line change regresses both axes simultaneously.

